 technology with a tremendous impact is clo...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 2&#10;domain: same_field&#10;radius: R1&#10;title: &amp;amp;lt;italic&amp;amp;gt;In situ&#10;&amp;amp;lt;/italic&amp;amp;gt;characterization of dynamic molecular&#10;behaviours at gas/liquid or liquid/liquid interfaces&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['In situ, time-resolved interrogation of&#10;dynamic gas/liquid or liquid/liquid interfaces', 'Interface-&#10;functionalized molecular luminescence tracing to make&#10;interfacial molecular states selectively observable', 'High-&#10;resolution and high-speed imaging for resolving rapidly&#10;moving, deformable interfacial regions', 'Strategies for&#10;separating weak interfacial signals from bulk-phase background&#10;under low signal-to-noise conditions', 'Linking angstrom-to-&#10;nanometer interfacial structural dynamics to larger-scale&#10;wetting, phase separation, emulsification, and transport&#10;phenomena']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s interface-selective&#10;luminescence-tracing and high-speed in situ imaging paradigm&#10;as a multimodal sensing architecture for operating multiphase&#10;interfaces, using environment-responsive probes to report&#10;local chemistry, temperature, flow, and transfer event...&#10;justification: The candidate paper addresses the same core&#10;bottleneck of observing weak, rapidly changing, heterogeneous&#10;interfacial phenomena in situ. Its transferable abstraction is&#10;not a specific instrument but an organizing principle: use&#10;interface-specific dynamic tracers and time-resol...&#10;abstract: &lt;p indent=&quot;0mm&quot;&gt;Gas/liquid and liquid/liquid&#10;interfaces, with their unique dynamic molecular behaviours&#10;such as high molecular reactivity, specific molecular&#10;enrichment, wide range of molecular motions, and distinctive&#10;molecular trajectories, have attracted significant researc...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Int