ange']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the SURFEX-style modular surface-&#10;platform abstraction to multiphase interfaces by defining a&#10;common interfacial state vector from multimodal nanoscale&#10;measurements and coupling submodels for structure, chemistry,&#10;charge transfer, flow, temperature, and mass/heat flux. Us...&#10;justification: Although SURFEX targets Earth surface modeling,&#10;its core abstraction—integrating heterogeneous surface&#10;variables into a coupled or offline framework that produces&#10;physically consistent fluxes—maps structurally onto the need&#10;to unify multimodal interfacial observables and upsca...&#10;abstract:" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f9cb9c;strokeColor=#b45f06;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="7996" width="620" height="3174" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step7_analogy_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step7_analogy_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step8" value="Step 8 Inspiration Selection&#10;status: completed&#10;selected_count: 3&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="11270" width="232" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step7_step_step8" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step_step8"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step8_selected_panel" value="Step 8 Selected Inspiration&#10;count: 3&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Integrating physics-based models with sensor data: An&#10;inverse modeling approach&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['inverse modeling that fuses physics-&#10;based models with sensor observations', 'estimation of hidden&#10;or unmeasured state variables from partial measurements',&#10;'physics-constrained data assimilation for multiscale&#10;inference', 'coupling local observables to macroscopic&#10;fluxes/rates through governing equations']&#10;combination_plan: Use an inverse-modeling/data-assimilation&#10;framework in which multiphase-interface physics models (mass,&#10;heat, charge, momentum, reaction transport) constrain and fuse&#10;heterogeneous modality-specific measurements, inferring&#10;unresolved nanoscale fields and connecting them to mac...&#10;justification: The candidate’s core abstraction—integrating&#10;physics-based models with sensor data via inverse&#10;modeling—directly addresses the original problem’s bottleneck&#10;of partial, modality-specific observables by providing a&#10;principled way to infer coupled hidden states and link local&#10;in...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 4&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Acceleration of uncertainty updating in the description&#10;of transport processes in heterogeneous materials&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Accelerated uncertainty updating for&#10;transport processes', 'Probabilistic inference or Bayesian&#10;updating in heterogeneous media', 'Uncertainty propagation&#10;across scales in coupled transport models', 'Data-model fusion&#10;under partial observability']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt accelerated uncertainty-updating&#10;methods from heterogeneous transport modeling to fuse&#10;multimodal interfacial measurements with physics-based&#10;transport models, enabling probabilistic inference of coupled&#10;nanoscale structure, chemical state, flow, temperature, and&#10;fluxes...&#10;justification: Although the candidate paper is from a&#10;different domain, its focus on accelerating uncertainty&#10;updating in heterogeneous transport processes provides a&#10;transferable abstraction for the original problem: multiphase&#10;interfaces are heterogeneous, partially observed systems&#10;where...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: earth_sciences&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Natural integration of scalar fluxes from complex&#10;terrain&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Conservative integration of&#10;heterogeneous scalar fluxes over complex boundaries',&#10;'Upscaling/local-to-global flux aggregation using spatial&#10;weighting or footprint concepts', 'Coordinate or geometric&#10;mapping from irregular local sources to macroscopic flux&#10;budgets']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the terrain-flux integration framework&#10;to multiphase interfaces by treating nanoscale structure,&#10;chemistry, heat/mass transfer, and flow measurements as&#10;spatially heterogeneous scalar flux contributions, then using&#10;conservative geometric/statistical upscaling to connect...&#10;justification: Although the candidate concerns complex terrain&#10;rather than multiphase interfaces, its core&#10;abstraction—integrating spatially heterogeneous scalar fluxes&#10;across a complex surface into a coherent macroscopic&#10;budget—maps directly onto the problem of linking local&#10;interfacial het...&#10;abstract:" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="11270" width="620" height="1500" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="12870" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Null-Flux Reciprocal Perturbation Microscopy for Measuring&#10;Nonlocal Interfacial Transport Kernels&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: Microscopic interface phenomena are currently&#10;measured as disconnected observables: structural layering by&#10;simultaneous neutron reflectivity, infrared spectroscopy, and&#10;ellipsometry [Author et al.,&#10;2022](https://openalex.org/W4308711154); local electrical and&#10;chemical-frictional heterogeneity by in situ conductive atomic&#10;force microscopy [Author et al.,&#10;2023](https://openalex.org/W4321480595); functional wettabili...&#10;methods: 1. Correlative operando interfacial cell: Build a&#10;liquid-solid cell with a planar silica, gold, or catalytic film,&#10;compatible with directional flow mapping [Author et al.,&#10;2020](https://openalex.org/W3028689404), in situ conductive&#10;atomic force microscopy [Author et al.,&#10;2023](https://openalex.org/W4321480595), and simultaneous&#10;reflectivity, infrared, and ellipsometry structural profiling&#10;[Author et al., 2022](https://openalex.org/W4308711154). For&#10;gas-liquid-solid extensions, add a controlled gas channel and&#10;ch...&#10;novelty_justification: The closest existing combination is the&#10;set of key references that together provide the proposed&#10;observables and operando context: directional liquid-solid flow&#10;mapping, in situ conductive AFM of local electrical/chemical&#10;heterogeneity, gas-liquid-solid wettability/mass-transfer&#10;characterization, and simultaneous structural profiling by&#10;neutron reflectivity, infrared spectroscopy, and ellipsometry.&#10;These reference...&#10;improvement_suggestions: [&quot;Sharpen the core mechanistic claim&#10;into a formal 'reciprocal null-manifold identifiability'&#10;theorem: specify which nonlocal, frequency-dependent interfacial&#10;kernels are uniquely recoverable from particular null-flux&#10;conditions under defined symmetry-breaking constraints, and&#10;prove that randomized or single-perturbation protocols cannot&#10;recover the same kernels.&quot;, 'Introduce a unique method-specific&#10;observable, such as phase-resolved null-cancellation surfaces or&#10;reciprocal null-flux quadrature signatures, that directly&#10;separates interfacial memory/nonlocality from bulk artifacts and&#10;provides a falsifiable prediction unavailable to passive or&#10;conventional active measurements.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="12870" width="680" height="906" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: in situ vibrational spectroscopy microscopy of&#10;reaction kinetics at gas-liquid and liquid-solid&#10;interfaces&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'situ vibrational', 'score': 10},&#10;{'text': 'vibrational spectroscopy', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'spectroscopy microscopy', 'score': 8}, {'text':&#10;'microscopy reaction', 'score': 7}, {'text': 'reaction&#10;kinetics', 'score': 6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Probing liquid/liquid interfaces at and away from&#10;equilibrium using vibrational sum frequency generation&#10;(2023) [score=0.8909]&#10;Abstract: The self-assembly and transport of species at&#10;oil/aqueous interfaces represent key mechanistic steps in&#10;processes spanning from liquid extraction to soft-matter&#10;neuromorphic electrical devices. While technologically and&#10;fundamentally important, there is a notable lack of&#10;chemi...&#10;&#10;2. Low energy electron diffraction (LEED) and sum&#10;frequency generation (SFG) vibrational spectroscopy&#10;studies of solid-vacuum, solid-air and solid-liquid&#10;interfaces (2002) [score=0.8812]&#10;Abstract: Electron based surface probing techniques can&#10;provide detailed information about surface structure or&#10;chemical composition in vacuum environments. The&#10;development of new surface techniques has made possible in&#10;situ molecular level studies of solid-gas interfaces and&#10;more recen...&#10;&#10;3. Determination of the Lewis acidity of&#10;amide–AlCl&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; based ionic liquid analogues by&#10;combined &lt;i&gt;in situ&lt;/i&gt; IR titration and NMR methods&#10;(2018) [score=0.7257]&#10;Abstract: A combinatorial method to determine both acidic&#10;strength and acidic amount of each Lewis acid site in&#10;amide-AlCl&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; based ionic liquid (IL) analogues&#10;was developed by the combination of &lt;i&gt;in situ&lt;/i&gt; IR&#10;titration and NMR analysis. &lt;sup&gt;31&lt;/sup&gt;P NMR was used to&#10;disti...&#10;&#10;4. In situ surface dynamics in heterogeneous catalysis&#10;(2004) [score=0.6611]&#10;Abstract: During the former half of the last century the&#10;mechanism of heterogeneous catalysis had been studied,&#10;keeping the catalyst in a black box, and on the basis of&#10;the information outside of the black box, it was discussed&#10;just from mere conjectures. The author initiated a method&#10;t...&#10;&#10;5. Review of: &quot;In situ Raman spectroscopy reveals the&#10;structure and